id: pm-web-5hdb
title: Refresh ADO and Jev catalog metadata after upstream manifest changes
description: Read-only comparison with the canonical fleet found that pm-ado now describes SDK import/export/sync and three-way reconciliation; pm-jev now includes the jev link command. The catalog and committed snapshot still carry the previous descriptions. Refresh metadata and commands together with regression evidence in a separate change.
type: Issue
status: in_progress
priority: 2
tags[2]: catalog,metadata
created_at: "2026-10-15T21:38:36.380Z"
updated_at: "2026-10-16T02:41:55.122Z"
author: codex-agent
acceptance_criteria: Catalog metadata and snapshot match the intended ADO and Jev manifests; live-fleet freshness and standalone release checks pass.
comments[14]{created_at,author,text}:
  "2026-10-15T23:00:14.611Z",codex-agent,Confirmed ADO import/export/sync and Jev link on package main. Extending the existing fleet snapshot generator and catalog tests to retain independent package command declarations in the committed fixture; both entries remain unreleased. No hosted changes.
  "2026-10-15T23:06:10.613Z",codex-agent,"The new all-package command receipt also found pre-existing omissions in CSV, GitHub, Jira, Linear, Ops, Presets, Review, Todos and VCS. Included metadata-only corrections required for complete command equality. The documented vcs layer local path remains an explicit dispatcher-backed exception. Snapshot generation reads manifest-selected TypeScript source in disposable copies via the pinned SDK; handlers never execute. The existing generator is reused."
  "2026-10-15T23:07:50.855Z",codex-agent,"Behavioral revert proof: kept the new snapshot and drift test intact, changed only the ADO catalog command array back to pm ado validate, and ran node --test --test-name-pattern=\"catalog commands match every package\" test/catalog.test.ts. Result: 1 test, 0 passed, 1 AssertionError naming pm-ado and missing export/import/sync, zero skipped. Restored original source bytes; identical command passed 1/1 with zero failures/skips. Canonical-fleet focused suite passed 24/24, including source-registration freshness."
  "2026-10-15T23:51:55.174Z",codex-agent,"Initial isolated npm release gate finished its suite at 597/605 pass, 7 fail, 1 cancelled, zero skips. All new catalog/snapshot checks passed, including canonical source command freshness. Existing Presets timeout/ENOTDIR and additional startup-deadline evidence are recorded on pm-web-qdhx; 31202 ms large-corpus graph read is recorded on pm-web-hqqp. Related partial worktree discovery follow-up is pm-web-4p94. No failing assertion or threshold changed. One unchanged npm retry will precede the independent Bun gate."
  "2026-10-16T00:02:16.682Z",codex-agent,"Final review found a coverage gap: the first command comparison checked 24 extensions but omitted the native Rust entry. Interrupted the unchanged npm retry before claiming any result. Added a separate native command receipt derived read-only from Cargo binary metadata and the README current native slice, including documented claim/release commands. The offline comparison now checks every one of the 25 catalog entries; native source freshness is also checked with the explicit fleet root. Full npm and Bun gates will run on this corrected final code."
  "2026-10-16T00:05:30.797Z",codex-agent,"Final all-entry receipt: PM-linked focused suite passes 25/25 with zero failures/cancellations/skips, including canonical extension and native source freshness. Repeated behavioral revert against the corrected guard: changing only the ADO command array back to pm ado validate fails 0/1 with missing export/import/sync; restoring exact source bytes passes 1/1 with zero skips. The regenerated receipts cover all 25 catalog identities: 237 SDK command paths across 24 extensions and eight README-declared native paths. Static type/lint/docstring checks and zero-duplication pass. Starting final isolated npm and Bun release gates at unchanged thresholds."
  "2026-10-16T00:42:19.747Z",codex-agent,"Final-code isolated npm release:check exits at coverage: 606 total, 603 passed, 2 failed, 1 cancelled, zero skipped. All command metadata, native receipt, drift and canonical freshness tests pass. Remaining existing deadline failures are source Presets (300000 ms), 2000-item graph read (16872 ms versus 10000 ms), and missing-database startup (10000 ms), recorded on pm-web-qdhx and pm-web-hqqp. S/L 90.90, branches 81.12, functions 94.17 are failed-run measurements at unchanged thresholds. Continuing with the independent Bun release gate."
  "2026-10-16T01:08:52.699Z",codex-agent,"Final independent Bun release:check exits at coverage: 604/606 pass, 1 fail, 1 cancelled, zero skips. Only existing built Presets timeout and following source spawn ENOTDIR fail; all new metadata/native/freshness tests and the graph latency assertion pass. Failed-run S/L 90.04, branches 80.73, functions 93.83 meet numeric thresholds, but both full gates remain blocked (npm 603/606). Running the downstream capacity/audit/packing/changelog/release-metadata checks independently before publishing the reviewable PR, with blocked gates explicit."
  "2026-10-16T01:15:06.462Z",codex-agent,"Final downstream checks pass independently: npm run accept:capacity 1/1 with zero skips; npm run audit:prod zero vulnerabilities; npm run pack:dry-run passes; npm run accept:packed accepts all four npm-current, bun-current, npm-minimum and bun-minimum scenarios; changelog:check, verify:release-changelog-date and verify:release-publish-attestation pass. Full aggregate gates remain failed: npm 603/606 (2 fail, 1 cancelled), Bun 604/606 (1 fail, 1 cancelled), both zero skipped. Focused PM-linked suite passes 25/25 and final ADO-only revert proof fails 0/1 then restores to 1/1. No threshold or failing deadline changed. Metadata implementation and independent receipts are ready for PR review, with existing timing blockers on pm-web-qdhx/pm-web-hqqp and partial-discovery follow-up pm-web-4p94. Releasing the claim; item stays in_progress for orchestrator verification."
  "2026-10-16T01:45:13.393Z",codex-agent,"Review round 1: reproduce the Cargo binary-table field-order rejection, scan each bin table through the next table header, and add real-file regressions for comments, field ordering, quote styles, multiple tables, and missing identity. Record behavioral revert proof, run unchanged npm and Bun release gates, then push and verify PR checks. origin/main is already an ancestor of the branch; no merge is needed."
  "2026-10-16T01:46:36.773Z",codex-agent,"Behavioral revert proof: with new regression fixtures retained, reverting only readNativeFleetCommands to HEAD makes node --test --test-name-pattern=\"native Cargo binary identity\" test/fleet-commands.test.ts exit 1: 12 total, 6 pass, 6 fail (five failing fixture cases plus their parent), zero cancelled/skipped. Failures cover reordered fields, comments/whitespace, matching later binary, single quotes, and a commented binary header incorrectly accepted. Restoring the exact fixed source bytes passes 12/12 with zero failures, cancellations or skips. The table scan stops at every following table header and keeps missing native identities fail-closed."
  "2026-10-16T01:46:59.511Z",codex-agent,"The linked regression command passes 12/12 with zero skips. pm test --run --only-last --progress also passes; this project disables automatic test-result recording, so results are recorded explicitly in comments. No test thresholds or deadlines changed. Full gates will use isolated HOME and disabled global/system Git configuration to reproduce CI identity; host load remains elevated, so npm and Bun will run sequentially."
  "2026-10-16T02:12:18.805Z",codex-agent,"Review round 1 focused catalog/fleet acceptance passes 37/37 with canonical fleet freshness enabled, zero failures/cancellations/skips. Isolated npm run release:check exits 0 at unchanged thresholds: coverage suite 618/618 pass, zero failures/cancellations/skips; measured statements/lines 90.94%, branches 81.13%, functions 94.17%. Capacity 1/1; production audit zero vulnerabilities; packed npm-current, bun-current, npm-minimum and bun-minimum all pass 4/4. Typecheck, lint, duplication, docstrings, packing, changelog, release-date and publish-attestation checks pass. Built/source HTTP acceptance passes at 226527/255199 ms versus unchanged 300000 ms deadlines; 2000-item graph read passes at 6352 ms versus unchanged 10000 ms. Starting sequential isolated Bun release gate."
  "2026-10-16T02:41:52.282Z",codex-agent,"Review round 1 isolated bun run release:check exits 0 at unchanged thresholds: coverage 618/618 passed, zero failures/cancellations/skips; statements/lines 90.89%, branches 81.10%, functions 94.17%. Capacity 1/1; production audit zero vulnerabilities; all four current/minimum npm/Bun packed consumers pass. Typecheck, lint, duplication, docstrings, packing, changelog, release-date and publish-attestation checks pass. Built/source HTTP acceptance passes at 246590/238125 ms versus unchanged 300000 ms deadlines; 2000-item graph read passes at 6716 ms versus unchanged 10000 ms. Both aggregate gates now pass. Cargo regression proof and linked 12/12 acceptance are recorded above; full focused suite passes 37/37. Only this item was touched; no new out-of-scope defect found. Releasing the claim with item in_progress for orchestrator verification; the code and append-only tracker history will be committed together, then PR checks monitored on the pushed head."
